as to macroeconomic conditionality  the spanish government does not believe  that we should use this  in order to sanction those countries  that cannot comply with economic  conditionality by taking away  structural funds  i mean this is something that will  impact all member states  this is not about the invasion of the  national sovereignty or taxation  sovereignty of over member states the  decision on own resources has to be  ratified by the national parliament so  this is absolutely  the domain of fiscal responsibility of  the member states this is not to grow  the budget in fact our budget in  relation to gni is falling down in  relation of what is now and what was in  the 90s so we are taking into account  the rigors and restraints of the present  present-day europe i believe it is our  responsibility to  translate the message from the european  council into the concrete steps and i  think that uh i have no doubts that the  the mff discussion this is a blueprint  for growth in europe until 20  until 2020.  we believe that the quality of spending  is important however better spending  should not mean  less spending  good results over negotiations would be  to reach an agreement where everyone is  equally unhappy  our  overarching challenge is to combine  budgetary consolidation with a growth  oriented reform and we need to do both  we need to find  the 100 billion savings in the  commission proposal we must stabilize  the budget  and i would refer  to the letter signed by several heads of  state already in the end of 2010  and we need to modernize our  expenditures and to spend it better  which means  we prioritize towards future challenges  competitiveness research and innovation  and internal security  but we have come a long way since  commission tabled its proposal since  last summer and it is of utmost  importance that we keep the pace up and  have an agreement by the end of this  year  on macroeconomic conditionality we  support measures to improve economic  governance but we don't support using  structure and cohesion funds as a  backdoor mechanism to circumvent our  agreements in that area  structure and cohesion funds need to be  used to the purpose they were intended  as economic convergence mechanisms  and i fear that using them as an  economic governance enforcement tool  undermines their purpose politicizes  their use and it doesn't respect member  state competence that was set out by the  van rompuy task force to which all 27 of  us agreed or protocol 15 of the treaties  due to the promotion of internal  development cohesion policy is an  economic growth facilitating policy  latvia's main concern is a problem of  capping in countries with a significant  gdp drop the tax proposal of the  presidency  goes in the right direction and we are  ready to continue its further  development  we think that the mff  should  economic growth thereby to create jobs  spending better spending well  and in the interest of citizens  then cohesion policy implementation  that policy is central in the union's  growth strategy and we need to apply it  in the best possible way thus  co-financing rates need to be set at the  current  levels at national level respecting the  restrictions that member states have to  contend with at the moment  also know that limiting expenditure is  the best guarantee of ensuring that  national transfers to the eu budget will  be kept under control  so all of this of course must be seen  subject to the condition that we reach  overall agreement we are nonetheless  prepared to continue making the biggest  net contribution but burden sharing must  be fairer and we need to therefore have  some sort of compensation  i think the discussions over the next  couple of months will allow us to  actually put things into practice we  can't just keep talking about  growth  forever in the day without actually  daring to  do something with the budget and i think  we do need to talk much more about our  investment policy in the eu we need to  have the means to achieve eu's important  goals  of growth cohesion and development  we cannot set ambitious goals as regards  the europe's 2020 strategy without  providing the necessary financial  instruments for the implementation  europe has to remain competitive and  coherent with its own agenda  let me start by saying that the  commission proposal can offer some  valuable contribution to sustainable  growth and employment  however given the need for  fiscal consolidation  we must be guided by the principle of  spending better rather than spending  more  on the cutting back on own resources  that will not help  again member states it will just  increase the gap between the different  regions which does not comply with the  objectives of the lisbon agenda  the european council  met last week to examine how we can turn  what we say about growth in europe into  concrete actions  and it's important important question uh  and the new mff has to be seen as a part  of the answer  that means providing ourselves with the  budget we need  one that is no bigger than is strictly  required  and but one that is consistent with our  goals and our ambitions  as regards the proposal  of macroeconomic conditionalities even  shall we understand the reasoning behind  this proposal  we cannot support these conditions in  their current form they're never ready  to discuss this issue further in a  constructive manner in order to make the  condition that is fair and limited in  the scope  we have to be ambitious in  the budget  so that we can attain the objectives  that we need in terms of growth and to  make sure that europe is put back on a  growth track and to make sure that we  are not faced with an everlasting  recession but at the same time we have  to make sure that the budget  contributions  allocated to the commission to attain  those objectives is reasonable  now we are  perfectly willing to examine the  proposals put forward by the commission  however we feel that this debate  should go beyond the terms of the  current debate we need to enter into  political commitments but look at  alternative proposals over the longer  term  we firmly believe  the next mff should be focused on  meeting eu 2020 strategy goals boosting  growth and employment  the main priorities of slovenia remain  unchanged cohesion policy and rural  development  i think it is important that we focus on  a better spending in order to improve  competitiveness and growth in the union  in these times of austerity this has to  be  achieved with the disciplined  mff i believe that having an honest  debate on the quality of spending in  connection with the need for solidarity  and convergence growth and jobs and  examining both the revenue and the  expenditure expenditure side in parallel  are important to reach an overall  balanced agreement  we also must focus on measures  contributing to growth which provides  european added value and we cannot  afford to do otherwise in this tough  financial economic situation  we need to stimulate growth and  employment and it is justified with  well-defined increases compared to  present period in research and  development and innovations in strategic  cross-border infrastructures in  environment and climate and as well as  security and external policy  we can consider it as a key that  cohesion policy should be better linked  to the eu 2020 goals and it should  support structural reforms therefore we  do share the aim that we need to spend  better however i also agree with those  who are saying that better spending does  not mean spending less and better  spending is a principle which applies to  all expenditure headings  malta considers the overall proposed  budget equation policy as the minimum  possible to address the present economic  social and territorial  it is important that cohesion policy is  focused on the less developed regions  and the regions exiting the convergence  objective  caucasian policies should focus on the  less developed regions and member states  in order to achieve economic social and  territorial cohesion  this means that  these countries will need more financing  in order to close the gap  while appreciating the need for the more  equitable distribution of direct  payments  we have to stress the fact that at the  beginning of the next mff croatia will  only start a long phasing in period that  will last well beyond 2020.  cuts on croatia's allocations at this  point would bring us further from fair  distribution in the first pillar  many of you insisted on the need to  enhance growth job and investment  through this mff  many also agreed that this mff should  ensure a better quality of expenditure  a number of you consider that these  principles should apply in all policy  areas  today we discussed for the first time  the revenue side we know that this part  will be an integral and very important  component of the final agreement
 

